workplan/2026-11-12-bidirectional-pipeline/tasks/T-035-skills-repair.md:63:   > - **A source's own "code" marking is root attribution, not a property of the figure.** A figure the source attributes to a code ("Code (required)", "per the building code") is recorded with `--root-type committee_assertion --root-ref-id <the code's ref_id>` when the code is held, else `--root-type untraced` with `--root-classification-basis` quoting the marking (precedent: extractions 57 and 64); it is presumed to echo the code and supplies no independent root (OR-19). The source's own pairing of a higher figure with the code figure beside it is an `extraction_relations` edge written with `relate-extraction`, never a label. Whether a figure is a floor or above it is derived against the regulatory stratum of the same parameter and jurisdiction, never typed; and no input row is stored as "best practice": best practice is the determination's output, the most accommodating value in the parameter's direction (`grep -n -F 'best practice = the best way to do something' references/project-standards.md`).
workplan/2026-11-12-bidirectional-pipeline/tasks/T-035-skills-repair.md:67:For items 2 to 4, the prose callers are `skills/run-pipeline_SKILL.md` and the two `add-extraction --help` strings in `scripts/db.py`; sweep `'=' for a point`, `for a point`, `lens-basis-text` and `best practice` (section 5) and correct any other sentence that states the opposite.
